    "explanation": "Rider, you are right about the ERP line and part of what you were charged comes back; Driver, the rest of the fare stands. This ruling was made without human review and either party may appeal it under POL-GEN-04.\n\nWhat the trip shows. EV-TRIP-02815, EV-GPS-02815 and EV-FARE-02815 all carry trip TRP-02815 and their pickup/start times agree, so the artifacts describe the same trip (POL-RD-08(a)). The trace is clean: 108 fixes at a 10-second interval, 100.0% coverage and no gaps, so it is NOT impaired under POL-RD-07(a) to (c) and may be relied on directly. The trace distance is 13.65 km against a booked optimal of 13.00 km, an excess of 0.65 km or 5.00%. That fails both POL-RD-01 establishment tests (more than 20% of optimal AND more than 0.80 km absolute), so no route deviation is established, the distance and time charges stand, and no POL-RD-02 recomputation runs. That answers both advocates' POL-RD-01 claims.\n\nThe ERP line. The fare charged 21.86 SGD in total, of which the single ERP line is 2.00 SGD for the 'AYE Alexandra Rd gantry'; the optimal route carries 0.00 ERP (optimal_route_erp_sgd = 0.0) and the off-optimal-route total is 2.00 SGD. The gantry's own coordinates (1.366147, 103.754636) are tested against the trace under POL-RD-09: the nearest fix is 6,130.08 m away (index 55, 2026-09-08T12:48:05+08:00) and no pair of consecutive fixes brackets the gantry. The 250 m crossing test is nowhere near met, so the trace does not place the vehicle at this gantry at all. Under POL-RD-09(4) a charge line for a gantry the trace never passes is a billing-integrity failure: the 2.00 SGD is refunded in full as a standalone correction, available whether or not a deviation exists. The route distance being only 5.00% over optimal does not defeat this, because POL-RD-09(4) does not depend on a deviation. This is a referral under POL-RD-09(4), not an escalation: POL-RD-10(8) expressly does not fire where the only unmatched line is one refunded under that limb, and no POL-RD-10 trigger otherwise applies (identifiers match; the trace is unimpaired; no timestamp conflicts; confidence is above 0.70).\n\nThe driver's answer. Your statement that 'the ERP is charged by the system' is an assertion that cites no evidence ID and no clause; under POL-RD-08 it carries no weight and does not discharge the driver's burden. No traffic advisory is on file either — EV-ADVIS-02815-01 is MISSING with weight 0.0 and issue MISSING_ARTIFACT, so POL-RD-03 could not be run — but because no party asserted a traffic cause against a cited advisory, POL-RD-13/POL-RD-10(5) is not engaged and this does not escalate the case. The rider's POL-RD-13 claim was discarded at the referee stage for citing the impaired advisory without disclosing its issue code, and that discard stands.\n\nProfiles. No repeat-deviation pattern is established: driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 0 against 388 completed trips, so POL-RD-06 does not apply and no conduct referral follows. The rider's deviation_claims_60d and deviation_claims_60d_substantiated are both 0, so the POL-RD-08 uplift is not engaged. Lifetime counters such as prior_deviation_flags, prior_no_show_flags and prior_disputes_upheld are context only under POL-GEN-01 and were not used as a ground of decision on either side.\n\nAmount and next steps. You placed the dispute at 4.00 SGD; the only line the evidence makes refundable is the 2.00 SGD ERP charge, so 2.00 SGD is returned and the balance stands — a partial refund. The fare's payment_status is CHARGED with refund_issued_sgd 0.00, so the money has not already been returned. The figure is already a multiple of SGD 0.05 and is at or below the SGD 8.00 execution threshold in POL-GEN-05, so it will execute automatically unless an appeal is lodged.\n\nConfidence is 0.90, above the 0.70 floor. The deciding fact — that the trace never crosses the charged gantry — is carried by two independent full-weight artifacts: EV-FARE-02815 (the charge line and the gantry's fixed coordinates, weight 1.0) and EV-GPS-02815 (the vehicle path, weight 1.0), so the POL-GEN-02(2) cap is 1.0 and no impairment discount applies."
  },
